the selected image, and Tesseract language-data caching fit the OCR purpose; no unrelated credential, profile, or broad filesystem access is requested.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Installation relies on npm and an unpinned caret dependency for tesseract.js, with no lockfile, so installs are not fully reproducible.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The instructions are scoped to OCR usage and options, but the prominent '100% local' wording is softened by notes that first use downloads language data.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No service, startup hook, agent memory write, privilege escalation, or long-running persistence is present; persistence is limited to normal dependency installation and Tesseract language-data cache behavior.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill’s stated purpose is image-to-text OCR using Tesseract.js, and the script only reads a user-supplied image path, runs OCR, and prints text or JSON results.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Before installing, consider whether your environment permits npm installs and first-run language-data downloads. For stricter or offline use, pin tesseract.js to a reviewed exact version, add a lockfile, prefetch or vendor language data, and avoid running installation or OCR as a privileged user.","findings":"[SDI-1] expected: The first-run language-data download is expected for Tesseract.js OCR and is disclosed in notes, though the '100% local' headline could be clearer for offline environments.\n[SQP-3] expected: PUBLISH.md is in Chinese, but it appears to be release documentation rather than runtime instructions that force a user's agent to use a language.\n[SQP-2] expected: README.md discloses first-run language-data downloads and caching; the disclosure is real but could be made more prominent as network/privacy guidance.\n[SC1] unexpected: The caret dependency and missing lockfile are not required for OCR functionality and reduce install reproducibility, but this is a supply-chain hygiene issue rather than evidence of malicious behavior.\n[SC4] unexpected: The unpinned tesseract.js dependency makes advisory status harder to verify from the artifact alone; users should prefer a pinned reviewed version and lockfile.\n[T08] unexpected: The static scan’s dependency concern is supported by package.json and PUBLISH.md, but no artifact evidence shows dependency confusion, embedded malicious code, or intentional unsafe behavior by the skill itself.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789177029507}}}}}